# Commit Message Format

When creating a commit, always include:

- A concise header summarizing the change.
- A body that explains the implementation and relevant behavior in detail.

Use a blank line between the header and body.

```text
Short description of the change

Detailed explanation of what changed, why it changed, and any important
implementation or verification details.
```
